            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0662" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.4016/158: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-17T14:00:00+01:00">March 17, 1939—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 17—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. My telegrams numbers 83, March 10, 7 p.m., and 89, March 15, 6 p.m. Ciano
                    assured me definitely today that his statement to me on March 10 held good so
                    far as concerns the time permitted foreign Jews to leave Italy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
